# Project summary

## 1) Agent — AI autonomy

**AI Autonomy Rule:** Never stop to present multiple-choice questions or ask for permission on routine implementation steps. Always automatically select the recommended path (Choice A) and execute directly unless a critical, blocking ambiguity arises.

Do not ask clarifying multiple-choice questions when intent is clear.


## 2) Postgres schema — no `public`

- **Do not use schema `public`.**
- Only schema: **`helloworldjunktest`**
- DB user: **`test_user1`** (superuser on Mac dev)
- Qualify tables in SQL and migrations: `helloworldjunktest.singles`, etc.

## 3) FE + BE on same web server (CORS)

**Frontend and backend always run on the same web server** — intentional same-origin model to avoid CORS issues.

- Production: FE + BE behind one HAProxy hostname.
- Mac dev: Vite `:3000` proxies `/api` to local BE (`API_PORT` / `DEV_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`).
- Do not hardcode cross-origin API URLs in production builds.

## 4) No session memory — Postgres only

**All mutable state must persist in PostgreSQL** (or cluster-wide Redis where already standardized).

- Requests are **round-robin load balanced** across a cluster — **no session pinning**.
- Do **not** use in-process `Map`, module-level session caches, or `express-session` in-memory stores for data that must be consistent across servers.
- Load user/profile state from DB on each request; write through Primary.

See `multi-server-stateless.mdc`.

## 5) Redis — centralized cache

Redis exists for **centralized cache** of a few shared, read-heavy items (rate limits when enabled, health, photo cache stats, etc.).

- Use **`REDIS_URL`** — not per-process memory — when cross-server fairness matters.
- Always TTL; fall back to DB if Redis is down.

See `cluster-architecture-redis.mdc`.

## 6) Postgres Primary + Replica

| Operation | Target |
|-----------|--------|
| **Writes** (`INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, DDL) | **Primary only** |
| **Reads** (`SELECT`, listings, profile loads) | **Local replica** on each app server (prod) |

After a write in the same request, use Primary or tolerate replication lag for read-your-writes.

See `postgres-primary-replica.mdc`.

## 7) Deployment topology (current vs future)

**Current (single box):** one server hosts HAProxy, Postgres Primary, Postgres Replica, and one web server (FE + BE).

**Future (multi-server):** ~5 servers splitting HAProxy, Primary, replicas, and web servers. Andrew will say when to target multi-server deploy — **until then, code must still follow cluster rules above** (stateless app servers, Primary writes, replica reads, Redis when shared).

See `cross-environment-deploy.mdc`.

## 8) Mac dev workflow

Bash init: **`source ~/b`** (repo copy: **`myscript/mac/b`**)

| Alias | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| **`feall`** | Frontend with hot reload (Vite) |
| **`beall`** | Backend with hot reload |
| **`deployall2`** | Mac → Ubuntu remote deploy (VPN + SSH) |
| **`showbuild`** | Print FE build stamp / checksum |

Env: `~/.ssh/be/.env` (BE), `fe/.env` (FE). Restart after env changes.

## 9) Ubuntu production workflow

Bash init: **`source ~/b`** (repo copy: **`myscript/ubuntu/b`**)

| Alias | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| **`work2`** | Interactive PM2 build + deploy |
| **`work2_deploy`** | Non-interactive work2 (SSH / deploy-all) |
| **`febeprod`** | PM2 build + deploy (alternate) |
| **`deployall`** | Deploy branch to all hosts in deploy-hosts.txt |
| **`showbuild`** / **`showartifact`** | Build stamp / deploy artifact checksum |

After BE env changes: `pm2 restart onlinemallwebsite`.

